{"author":"RebarBotNava","author_email":"joeoakhart+bot@navapbc.com","author_id":"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d","author_sig":"{\"payload\": \"\", \"payloadType\": \"application/vnd.rebar.authorship.v1+json\", \"signatures\": [{\"keyid\": \"594c-9dcf-5ad6-4e6d\", \"sig\": \"\"}]}","data":{"fields":{"description":"## Context / Problem\nEighteen Python modules under `tests/unit` contain 43 audited prose blocks: 22 leading docstrings and 21 full-line comments. Scope was revalidated against `origin/main@9e6a0e436520f67962c22dc244d7b4f77f5bee45`. Since the original audit, the nested-pytest basetemp guard, close-precheck helper name, and failed-call seam changed; this plan preserves their current forms. The vague `test_ticket_project_fields.py:1-13 and held-out narration` scope is replaced by exact IDs.\n\n## Approach\nEdit only the stable-ID blocks below. Capture immutable before/final blobs for every owned path and parse both with `ast.parse(..., type_comments=True)`. On comparison copies, remove only an allowlisted leading `Expr(Constant(str))` that is the first statement of a `Module`, `ClassDef`, `FunctionDef`, or `AsyncFunctionDef`; normalize only `ast.TypeIgnore.lineno`; require the remaining normalized ASTs to match.\n\nTokenize both blobs and reject every changed inline comment or non-allowlisted full-line comment. Preserve non-docstring runtime strings, regexes, prompts, imports, decorators, annotations, assertions, subprocess arguments, test data, shebangs, and complete directive-bearing physical lines exactly. Adjacent blank-line normalization is allowed only around an edited block.\n\n## Stable block allowlist\n- `tests/unit/test_sync_narrow_refspec.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_sync_union_recovery.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_tests_import_convention.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_threshold_recalibration.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_throttle_no_failover_1c0d.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_ticket_project_fields.py` — 14 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_three_states_are_distinguishable_after_replay`\n  - `C:test_three_states_are_distinguishable_after_replay:before:assert absent.get(\"bridge_project\") is None`\n  - `C:test_three_states_are_distinguishable_after_replay:before:assert absent.get(\"bridge_project\") != empty[\"bridge_project\"]`\n  - `C:test_three_states_are_distinguishable_after_replay:before:assert absent.get(\"repos\") == []`\n  - `C:test_bridge_project_and_repos_are_parity_across_surfaces:before:cli_id = _created_id`\n  - `C:test_bridge_project_and_repos_are_parity_across_surfaces:before:lib_id = rebar.create_ticket`\n  - `C:test_bridge_project_and_repos_are_parity_across_surfaces:before:mcp_tools: dict = {}`\n  - `D:test_mcp_edit_sets_bridge_project_and_repos_at_parity`\n  - `C:test_promote_only_refuses_rebind_but_allows_first_set:before:unbound = _created_id`\n  - `C:test_promote_only_refuses_rebind_but_allows_first_set:before:bound = _created_id`\n  - `D:test_legacy_create_event_replays_with_new_keys_defaulted`\n  - `C:test_legacy_create_event_replays_with_new_keys_defaulted:before:assert state[\"ticket_type\"] == \"task\"`\n  - `C:test_legacy_create_event_replays_with_new_keys_defaulted:before:assert state.get(\"bridge_project\") is None`\n- `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget_headroom.py` — 3 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_MEASURED_SLOWEST_LEGITIMATE_CALL_SECS = 29.93`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_REQUIRED_HEADROOM = 2.0`\n- `tests/unit/test_timeout_budget.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_transition_close.py` — 5 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:@pytest.fixture`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def _status_events`\n  - `C:<module>:before:_GATE_ON`\n  - `C:<module>:before:def test_text_output_warns_when_a_close_lands_without_its_signature`\n- `tests/unit/test_transition_force_flag_24f7.py` — 7 blocks:\n  - `D:<module>`\n  - `C:<module>:before:EXEMPT = {`\n  - `C:<module>:before:\"scripts/build_cloud_adf_corpus.py\"`\n  - `C:<module>:before:\"scripts/build_dc_wiki_corpus.py\"`\n  - `C:<module>:before:\"docs/experiments/plan-review-gate/fixtures/eval_specs/plan-review-T6.eval.yaml\"`\n  - `D:_tracked_files`\n  - `D:test_retired_spelling_is_absent_from_every_tracked_file`\n- `tests/unit/test_transport_retry_jitter.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_transport_retry.py`: `D:test_midrun_429_self_heals_without_duplicate_comment`\n- `tests/unit/test_trusted_env_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_trusted_env.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_typecheck_scope.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_unique_cache_writes.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_unsigned_env_fsck_heldout.py`: `D:<module>`\n- `tests/unit/test_usage_log_failed_calls.py`: `D:<module>`\n\n`D:<symbol>` is a true leading docstring. `C:<scope>:before:<code>` is one maximal contiguous full-line block before unchanged code. No other prose is editable.\n\n## Protected false positives\nKeep exact three already-concise behavioral docstrings in `test_ticket_project_fields.py`: `D:test_three_states_are_distinguishable_after_replay`, `D:test_bridge_project_and_repos_are_parity_across_surfaces`, and `D:test_promote_only_refuses_rebind_but_allows_first_set`. Also keep exact the force-exemption comments before the frozen `e6_selfconsistency_inputs.jsonl` cohort, `CHANGELOG.md`, and this test file; they are short, load-bearing reasons rather than bloat.\n\n## Preserved contracts and consumers\n- Sync keeps explicit narrow-refspec fetch, provenance-based union/adopt, orphan refusal, reachability, and aggressive-gc safety.\n- Import/typecheck/threshold guards keep bare-pytest behavior, scripts scope, every approved threshold/posture, and the new isolated basetemp.\n- Ticket fields keep absent/empty/key states, CLI/library/MCP parity, promote-only refusal, legacy defaults, and a clear held-out boundary.\n- Timeout coverage keeps full-phase enforcement, the 29.93-second measured floor, 2x headroom, thread-watchdog failure mode, and marker overrides.\n- Close/force coverage keeps quiet commit matching, current `close_precheck._referencing_commits`, durable signing/force/provenance causes, text warnings, one reason-bearing force option, loud retired-spelling rejection, and exact exemptions.\n- Retry/trust/cache/usage coverage keeps equal jitter, below-agent-loop no-duplicate retry, most-recoverable throttle classification, pinned-key/era checks, unique atomic writes, unsigned-writer detection, and current `run_shape()` failed-call logging.\n- All owned modules are direct pytest inputs. `test_ci_workflow_parity.py` explicitly collects the import/timeout guards; `test_nested_pytest_uniqueness.py` scans the bare-pytest launch; the force test scans tracked source. No target import, `__doc__`, `inspect.getdoc`, or pydoc consumer was found.\n\n## Acceptance Criteria\n- [ ] Only declared stable-ID blocks and adjacent blank lines change; normalized-AST and token/comment comparisons pass on every owned path.\n- [ ] Every edited block is shorter and retains its listed current contract while removing chronology, duplication, obvious narration, or separator ornament.\n- [ ] An independent reviewer posts one leaf-linked TSV row per block: `stable_block_id<TAB>before_citation<TAB>final_citation<TAB>preserved_contract_or_consumer<TAB>directives_exact<TAB>before_words<TAB>after_words<TAB>semantic-preservation<TAB>bloat-removal<TAB>reviewer_session`.\n- [ ] Every expected row has immutable citations and `directives_exact=PASS`, `semantic-preservation=PASS`, and `bloat-removal=PASS`; missing/failing rows block closure.\n- [ ] All five structured verify commands pass.\n\n## Verification\nThe five DD-level commands recorded on this ticket run focused pytest (including named consumers), scoped Ruff check plus format-check, comment hygiene, owned-path `git diff --check`, and worktree-venv `make verify`. They are the executable completion oracle.\n"}},"env_id":"b8a354e0-12c3-4cf2-bbf1-fcc9685d5126","event_typ